cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuadForge or the FORGE engine, please cite it as below."
title: "QuadForge Vivaldi: a Blender add-on with the FORGE quad remeshing engine"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "GregCarreno3D"
    email: "gregcarr3dwork@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gregcarreno3d-dev/quadforge-vivaldi"
url: "https://github.com/gregcarreno3d-dev/quadforge-vivaldi"
abstract: >-
  QuadForge is a Blender add-on for quad and triangle remeshing. Its engine, FORGE, is a dependency-free C++17
  program that computes a smooth four-direction cross field, a seamless integer-grid parametrization and a quad
  extraction, with exact symmetry, hard-edge preservation, zones and density control. See docs/TECHNICAL_REPORT.md.
keywords:
  - remeshing
  - quad meshing
  - retopology
  - cross field
  - integer-grid map
  - Blender
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.14.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
